Subject: [PATCH v1 0/2] media: i2c: add Samsung S5KGW1P sensor driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Samsung S5KGW1P (ISOCELL GW1) is a 64MP CMOS image sensor connected
over a 3-trio MIPI CSI-2 C-PHY bus. It is the main camera of the Samsung
Galaxy A52 4G (a52q, SM7125).

This series adds a device tree binding and a V4L2 sub-device driver for
it, built on the v4l2-cci register accessors. The register tables were
decoded from the vendor CamX sensor module. A 2x2-binned 4624x3468 mode
at 30 fps and a 4x4-binned 2000x1128 mode up to 120 fps are supported.

Note the C-PHY bus: capturing from this sensor needs MIPI C-PHY support
in the receiver (camss), which is not yet in mainline. The sensor
endpoint declares bus-type = <4> (CSI-2 C-PHY).

Tested on the Galaxy A52 with libcamera (simple pipeline, camss) on a
downstream 6.14 kernel with an out-of-tree camss C-PHY patch; the sensor
register tables are unchanged since.

